  "chapter": {
    "number": 142,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(143) A Psalm of David, when his son pursued him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, attend to my prayer: listen to my supplication in your truth; hear me in your righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And enter not into judgment with your servant, for in your sight shall no man living be justified.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the enemy has persecuted my soul; he has brought my life down to the ground; he has made me to dwell in a dark place, as those that have been long dead.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore my spirit was grieved in me; my heart was troubled within me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I remembered the days of old; and I meditated on all your doings: yes, I meditated on the works of your hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I spread forth my hands to you; my soul thirsts for you, as a dry land. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear me speedily, O Lord; my spirit has failed; turn not away your face from me, else I shall be like to them that go down to the pit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cause me to hear your mercy in the morning; for I have hoped in you; make known to me, O Lord, the way wherein I should walk; for I have lifted up my soul to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me from my enemies, O Lord; for I have fled to you for refuge.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Teach me to do your will; for you are my God; your good Spirit shall guide me in the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 256
          },
          {
            "text": "straight way.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall quicken me, O Lord, for your name's sake; in your righteousness you shall bring my soul out of affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And in your mercy you will destroy my enemies, and will destroy all those that afflict my soul; for I am your servant.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 256,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. as Heb. 'land of uprightness.'",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 142,
          "verse": 10
        }
      }
    ]
  },
